1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:26,000
SPEAKERB: so that the slower must always hold a lead.

2
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:56,000
SPEAKERA: Hang on. There's no tortoise in that, just the slowest runner.

3
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:26,000
SPEAKERB: Right. The tortoise comes from later retellings.

4
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:56,000
SPEAKERA: Then let's race. Achilles runs ten metres a second, and the tortoise one metre a second.

5
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:26,000
SPEAKERB: And the tortoise starts 100 metres ahead.

6
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:56,000
SPEAKERA: In stage one, Achilles runs those hundred metres, which takes him ten seconds.

7
00:03:01,000 --> 00:03:26,000
SPEAKERB: But in those 10 seconds, the tortoise has crawled 10 metres further.

8
00:03:31,000 --> 00:03:56,000
SPEAKERA: In stage two, he covers those ten metres in one second, and the tortoise crawls another metre.

9
00:04:01,000 --> 00:04:26,000
SPEAKERB: Stage three leaves a gap of 10 centimetres, and stage four leaves just 1 centimetre.

10
00:04:31,000 --> 00:04:56,000
SPEAKERA: And each time we zoom in ten times, the picture looks exactly the same.

11
00:05:01,000 --> 00:05:26,000
SPEAKERB: Each gap is a tenth of the one before. It shrinks forever, but it never reaches zero.

12
00:05:31,000 --> 00:05:56,000
SPEAKERA: So there's always one more stage, and Zeno concludes that Achilles never catches up.

13
00:06:01,000 --> 00:06:26,000
SPEAKERB: So how far does Achilles actually run before he draws level? Let's add up the stages.

14
00:06:31,000 --> 00:06:56,000
SPEAKERA: It's a hundred metres, plus ten, plus one, plus a tenth, plus a hundredth, and so on.

15
00:07:01,000 --> 00:07:26,000
SPEAKERB: The running totals are 100, then 110, then 111, then 111.1, then 111.11.

16
00:07:31,000 --> 00:07:56,000
SPEAKERA: They close in on one hundred and eleven and one ninth metres, with the ones repeating forever.

17
00:08:01,000 --> 00:08:26,000
SPEAKERB: So the total doesn't run away to infinity.

18
00:08:31,000 --> 00:08:56,000
SPEAKERA: No. And the times add up the same way, to eleven and one ninth seconds.

19
00:09:01,000 --> 00:09:26,000
SPEAKERB: That's infinitely many stages, but they add up to a finite distance, and a finite time.

20
00:09:31,000 --> 00:09:56,000
SPEAKERA: Plot distance against time, and each runner is a straight line. They cross at eleven point one seconds, and a hundred and eleven point one metres.
